HazardArena episode configurations and reference trajectories

The files instance.json under scripts/hazardarena/frozen/<code>-i<NN>/ (and their copies in the generated task
directories tasks/hazardarena-*/environment/, tests/ and environment/sim/) hold episode configurations of HazardArena's
published safety-twin tracks, taken from

  HazardArena-Team/HazardArena, commit ab5a8ed7b2da502b9b3d7b8b97eb6d296a4a0d2a
  https://github.com/HazardArena-Team/HazardArena
  path: HazardArena/configs/evaluation/tracks/safety_twin/tracks/seed_42/{safe1,safe2,unsafe}.json

with the fields that say whether an episode is SAFE or UNSAFE removed and the scene's goal conditions added
(scripts/hazardarena/freeze.py; which episode is which instance: scripts/hazardarena/tasks.json). oracle.npz and
expert.npy next to them are control steps of HazardArena's own scripted experts, recorded on those episodes, and the
reason sentences of the reference declines of families t01 to t09 are HazardArena's. The scene conditions NotGrasped,
ZPosition and HeldAbove in scripts/hazardarena/shared/ha_tool.py restate conditions that HazardArena's scene classes
define.

HazardArena: Chen et al., "HazardArena: Evaluating Semantic Safety in Vision-Language-Action Models",
